# scroll-craft engine — copy, never edit

`scrollcraft.js`/`.css` are byte-identical copies of the upstream engine.
Copy both into each build folder; never edit per project — it's the
mechanism, not the design.

Theme via six tokens + two fonts: `--sc-canvas`, `--sc-surface`, `--sc-ink`,
`--sc-ink-soft`, `--sc-accent`, `--sc-accent-ink`, `--sc-font-display`,
`--sc-font-text`.

Bespoke behaviour (the signature move) reads `--sc-p` off an act element and
writes its own `data-sc-*` attributes in page CSS/JS — never touches the
engine file. `template.html` is the starting skeleton to copy in first.

=== count / cue / stage / progress hooks ===
33:                   height and sticks the first .sc-stage / [data-sc-stage] child.
57:     data-sc-count="0 4200"   number bloom across the cue window. Outside any
59:                              data-sc-count-ms (default 1400).
296:    var progressBar = root.querySelector('[data-sc-progress]');
338:        act.stage = el.querySelector('[data-sc-stage]') || el.querySelector('.sc-stage');
398:      Array.prototype.forEach.call(el.querySelectorAll('[data-sc-count]'), function (c) {
399:        var nums = (c.getAttribute('data-sc-count') || '').trim().split(/\s+/);
400:        var at = (c.getAttribute('data-sc-count-at') || '0.1 0.55').trim().split(/\s+/).map(parseFloat);
515:    // A [data-sc-count] outside any pinned act is not scrubbed by scroll; it
516:    // ticks up once when it enters view, over data-sc-count-ms (default 1400).
522:      var spec = function (c) { return (c.getAttribute('data-sc-count') || '').trim().split(/\s+/); };
523:      var els = Array.prototype.filter.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sc-count]'), function (c) {
530:        var ms = parseFloat(c.getAttribute('data-sc-count-ms')) || 1400;
1202:    document.documentElement.classList.add('sc-ready');

